-- int-tests-counting: the cross-group consistency register, part 1: HOW EACH GROUP COUNTS THE DAYS OF A PERIOD, run on the same anchor days.
-- Each group registered a fork on the counting convention of its own periods. The question here is whether the nine readings TAKEN are one convention. They are two, and each applies where the Law's words put it:
--   (1) A period "after an event" or "from a notice" (retention for 10 years after deregistering, a year of retention, 28 days from the notice, 7 days after it is made, 14 days after a termination, 14 days before an appointment):
--       the day of the event is NOT counted. The last day is the event day plus N; a period of years ends on the anniversary; 29 February falls back to 28 February (daydate's `add years` and `add months` clamp).
--       Used by G3 (F3.4), G6 (F6.18, F6.14), G8 (F8.7, F8.9, F8.10, F8.12), G7 (F7.2), G9 (F9.1, F9.5, F9.7), G4 (F4.9), G2 (F2.6), G5 (F5.10).
--   (2) A period that BEGINS on a named day (a term of office from its first day; an order of the court from the first day named; a text in force from the day named; an absence of days): the named day IS counted.
--       Used by G9 (F9.2, F9.4), G5 (F5.9), G7 (F7.11). A term of 6 years from 1 March ends (the person is no longer appointed) on the 1 March 6 years later, one day EARLIER in terms of the last day served than family (1) would put it.
--   (3) A period BACKWARD from an event ("the 12 months preceding the application", "the most recent year"): the day of the event is outside (G4 F4.1, G3 F3.7).
-- The expected values were decided by hand from these conventions before the module was run; each assertion names the group whose convention it exercises.

§ `Integration layer -- consistency register: counting`

GIVETH A `Readings of the fleet`
fleet MEANS `Int the favoured readings of the fleet`

§§ `Family (1): after an event, the day of the event is not counted -- anchor 15 June 2026 (an ordinary day)`

GIVETH A `Registered charity`
`the school company as the register holds it` MEANS
    `Int IP7 the registered charity` fleet (`Int IP5 the entity` fleet `the text of 2 October 2026` EMPTY (YMD 2026 10 2) `Int fx the registered school company`) `Int fx the register entry of the school company`

GIVEN received IS A DATE @desc The day the copy was received
GIVETH A `Copy held by the Commissioner (Article 8(6))`
`a constitution received on` received MEANS
    `Copy held by the Commissioner (Article 8(6))` WITH kind IS `the constitution of the charity, or an amendment to it`, `date received or made` IS received, `date it ceased to be operative` IS NOTHING

GIVEN notice IS A DATE @desc The day of the deregistration notice
GIVETH A `Deregistration of the entity`
`a deregistration by notice on` notice MEANS
    `Deregistration of the entity` WITH
        route IS `by written notice under Article 16(1) on the ground that the entity no longer meets the charity test`
        `date of the deregistration` IS notice
        `date of the preliminary notice` IS NOTHING
        `the Commissioner is satisfied that the grounds have existed since` IS NOTHING
        `past date specified in the deregistration notice` IS NOTHING
        `past date specified in the preliminary notice` IS NOTHING
        `the Commissioner determines that the deregistration takes effect retrospectively` IS FALSE

-- Ten years of retention: G3 (Article 8(6), a copy) and G6 (Article 17(1)(a), the information registered) both take the day of the event as not counted: the last day is 15 June 2036, the first day of discard 16 June 2036.
#ASSERT `Art 8(6) the Commissioner may discard the copy on` (`Int the reading of Articles 8 to 10` `the calendar year`) (`a constitution received on` (YMD 2026 6 15)) `the school company as the register holds it` EQUALS `the copy may be discarded on and after` OF (YMD 2036 6 16)
#ASSERT `Art 17(1)(a) the Commissioner may discard the information on` (`Int the reading of Articles 15 to 20` `calendar months`) (`a deregistration by notice on` (YMD 2026 6 15)) EQUALS YMD 2036 6 16
#ASSERT `Art 17(1)(a) the last day on which the Commissioner must retain the information` (`Int the reading of Articles 15 to 20` `calendar months`) (`a deregistration by notice on` (YMD 2026 6 15)) EQUALS YMD 2036 6 15
-- G8: a document retained for a year (Article 26(5)(a)): provided 15 June 2026, no proceedings: the last day is 15 June 2027 (the day provided is not counted).
GIVETH A `Facts of the retention of a document under Article 26(5)`
`a document provided on 15 June 2026 with no proceedings` MEANS
    `Facts of the retention of a document under Article 26(5)` WITH `day the document was provided or retained` IS YMD 2026 6 15, `day of the notice` IS YMD 2026 6 1, `day proceedings were commenced` IS NOTHING, `day proceedings concluded` IS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 26(5) the Commissioner may keep the document until` (`Int the reading of Articles 26 to 36` `calendar months`) `a document provided on 15 June 2026 with no proceedings` EQUALS `retention is permitted up to and including` OF (YMD 2027 6 15)
-- G8: a period fixed by a notice served on 15 June 2026 of 30 days (Article 26(1)): the last day is 15 July 2026; an appeal limit of 28 days from the notice (Article 36(2)): 13 July 2026.
#ASSERT `Art 26(1) the last day allowed by the notice` (`Int the reading of Articles 26 to 36` `calendar months`) (`a period of days fixed by the notice` 30) (YMD 2026 6 15) EQUALS YMD 2026 7 15
#ASSERT `Art 36(2) the last day to bring the appeal` (`Int the reading of Articles 26 to 36` `calendar months`) (`Dates of an appeal under Article 36(2)` WITH `day of the decision` IS YMD 2026 6 10, `day of the notice of the decision` IS JUST (YMD 2026 6 15), `day the appeal was lodged` IS YMD 2026 7 1) 28 EQUALS YMD 2026 7 13
-- G7: an instrument made on 15 June 2026 and in force 7 days after: 22 June 2026 (the day of making left out).
#ASSERT `Endnotes: the day an instrument made on a day comes into force 7 days after` (YMD 2026 6 15) `the favoured interpretation` EQUALS YMD 2026 6 22
-- G9: a notice before an appointment on 15 June 2026 must be given at least 2 weeks before: the latest day is 1 June 2026; a notice after a termination on 15 June 2026 within 2 weeks: the latest day is 29 June 2026.
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the latest day for a notice of intention before an appointment` (`Int the reading of Schedules 1 and 2` `calendar months`) (YMD 2026 6 15) 2 EQUALS YMD 2026 6 1
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the latest day for a notice of a termination` (`Int the reading of Schedules 1 and 2` `calendar months`) (YMD 2026 6 15) 2 EQUALS YMD 2026 6 29
-- G4: the period for the Commissioner's decision starts the day after the date of the application (F4.9); the twelve months preceding an application lodged on 15 June 2026 end the day before it.
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the twelve months preceding the application` (`Int the reading of Articles 11 and 12`) (`Int fx a complete application lodged on` (YMD 2026 6 15)) EQUALS `Period of days` OF (YMD 2025 6 15), (YMD 2026 6 14)

§§ `Family (2): from a named day, that day is counted -- anchor 15 June 2026`

-- G9: a term of office of 6 years from 15 June 2026 EXPIRES on 15 June 2032 (the first day on which the person is no longer appointed): the last day served is 14 June 2032. The same arithmetic in family (1) (10 years of retention)
-- ends on the anniversary itself and is discarded the day after. The two differ by one day by design: "the period for which the person is appointed expires" against "retain for 10 years after deregistering".
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the latest end date of a term of an appointment` (`Int the reading of Schedules 1 and 2` `calendar months`) (YMD 2026 6 15) 6 EQUALS YMD 2032 6 15
-- G5: an order of the court for a specified period of 30 days whose first day named is 15 June 2026 is in operation on 14 July 2026 (the 30th day) and not on 15 July 2026.
GIVETH A `Period of an order of the court`
`a specified period of 30 days from 15 June 2026` MEANS `a specified period` OF (YMD 2026 6 15), 30
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the order is in operation on the day` (`Int the reading of Articles 13 and 14` `the calendar year`) `a specified period of 30 days from 15 June 2026` (YMD 2026 6 15)
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the order is in operation on the day` (`Int the reading of Articles 13 and 14` `the calendar year`) `a specified period of 30 days from 15 June 2026` (YMD 2026 7 14)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(3) the order is in operation on the day` (`Int the reading of Articles 13 and 14` `the calendar year`) `a specified period of 30 days from 15 June 2026` (YMD 2026 7 15)

§§ `29 February: every group that adds a year or a month clamps to the last day of the month (daydate add years and add months) -- anchor 29 February 2024`

#ASSERT `Art 8(6) the Commissioner may discard the copy on` (`Int the reading of Articles 8 to 10` `the calendar year`) (`a constitution received on` (YMD 2024 2 29)) `the school company as the register holds it` EQUALS `the copy may be discarded on and after` OF (YMD 2034 3 1)
#ASSERT `Art 17(1)(a) the last day on which the Commissioner must retain the information` (`Int the reading of Articles 15 to 20` `calendar months`) (`a deregistration by notice on` (YMD 2024 2 29)) EQUALS YMD 2034 2 28
GIVETH A `Facts of the retention of a document under Article 26(5)`
`a document provided on 29 February 2024 with no proceedings` MEANS
    `Facts of the retention of a document under Article 26(5)` WITH `day the document was provided or retained` IS YMD 2024 2 29, `day of the notice` IS YMD 2024 2 1, `day proceedings were commenced` IS NOTHING, `day proceedings concluded` IS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 26(5) the Commissioner may keep the document until` (`Int the reading of Articles 26 to 36` `calendar months`) `a document provided on 29 February 2024 with no proceedings` EQUALS `retention is permitted up to and including` OF (YMD 2025 2 28)
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the latest end date of a term of an appointment` (`Int the reading of Schedules 1 and 2` `calendar months`) (YMD 2024 2 29) 6 EQUALS YMD 2030 2 28
-- G4: the twelve months preceding an application lodged on 29 February 2028 start on 28 February 2027 (a year before 29 February is 28 February: F4.6) and end the day before the application, 28 February 2028.
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the twelve months preceding the application` (`Int the reading of Articles 11 and 12`) (`Int fx a complete application lodged on` (YMD 2028 2 29)) EQUALS `Period of days` OF (YMD 2027 2 28), (YMD 2028 2 28)

§§ `Months: G9 clamps (the favoured F9.3 and F9.7 reading) and the rolled reading is the callable alternative -- anchor 30 November 2026`

-- A resignation on not less than 3 months' notice given on 30 November 2026: there is no 30 February, so the earliest day it can take effect is 28 February 2027 (clamped); rolled it would be 2 March 2027.
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the earliest day a notice of resignation can name` (`Int the reading of Schedules 1 and 2` `calendar months`) (YMD 2026 11 30) 3 EQUALS YMD 2027 2 28
#ASSERT `F9.3 reading C: the earliest day a resignation can take effect, the months being rolled` (YMD 2026 11 30) 3 EQUALS YMD 2027 3 2
